//? Title: Shortest common supersequences: actual LCS cells and reverse emissions
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given two integer sequences, construct a shortest sequence containing both as
subsequences. A two-by-two example makes the LCS table and native backtracking
visible before the original fixtures.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Let L(i,j) be the LCS length of the first i and j values. Its zero borders are
zero. Matching values give L(i,j)=1+L(i-1,j-1); otherwise take
max(L(i-1,j),L(i,j-1)). Matching tails emit once; an unequal tie emits from the
first input. Each shared emission saves one position, so
$$ |SCS(A,B)|=|A|+|B|-L(n,m). $$
\alttext(The shortest common supersequence length equals the sum of input lengths minus the longest common subsequence length.)
Any supersequence aligns at most L common occurrences, giving the lower bound;
the actual backtrack attains it. This full-table method takes O(n*m) time and
storage, plus linear output. The displayed emission history is reverse order.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/scs_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/shortest_common_supersequence.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::shortest_common_supersequence_trace({1, 2}, {2, 3});
    std::print("Actual LCS table `{}`; actual forward SCS `{}`.\n\n| remaining first | remaining second | " "emitted |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               r.table, r.sequence);
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", s.first_size, s.second_size, s.value);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Input [1,2] and [2,3]");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual LCS length {}", r.lcs_length));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual output {}", r.sequence));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/scs_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Actual LCS table `[[0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0], [0, 1, 1]]`; actual forward SCS `[1, 2, 3]`.

| remaining first | remaining second | emitted |
| ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 2 | 2 | 3 |
| 2 | 1 | 2 |
| 1 | 0 | 1 |
\image(figures/scs_tiny.svg)
// result_end
